  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation is the clear best (0.6530), far exceeding image-only (0.208) and other RNA encoders. The critical open question is whether fusing the weak image signal with the strong RNA multiprofile representation can push accuracy above 0.65, or whether the weak image features will dilute the RNA signal. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the most direct logical extension of our best result, changing only the model setting from rna_only to multimodal with concat fusion. It isolates the effect of adding the image modality to the proven-best RNA pipeline. If it improves over 0.6530, the remaining 3 experiments can explore fusion strategy (weighted) and image encoder (ViT-L); if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can focus remaining budget on marginal refinements. This is the highest-information experiment given the 3-experiment remaining budget."
